# Execution rules

## Cron only, no queue workers

Production is shared hosting with a single cron entry running `php artisan schedule:run` every minute. Do not add a queue worker, a daemon, or code that assumes one is running.

## The scheduler is the clock, project schedules are data

The Laravel scheduler only ticks. A dispatch command queries projects whose `next_run_at` has passed, claims each one atomically, and runs it inline within a time budget. Guard the scheduled entry with `withoutOverlapping()`.

## Run now never executes in a web request

A manual run marks the project as due so the next tick picks it up. HTTP requests must not perform provider fetches or publishing.

## Timezones are domain data

Resolve a schedule against the organization timezone, overridden by the project timezone when set. Never use the server timezone or the viewer's current timezone, and use Carbon for all DST-aware arithmetic.
